# Conveyor-belt transport on a named closed loop.  This is the general control model:
# unlike Cyclone it assigns no data/ancilla roles and promises no two-rotation schedule.
# Its architecture-specific rules are the standard transport rules themselves, because a
# conveyor earns no exception from one waveform, one direction, or rail ordering.

ruleset "conveyor"
title "Conveyor-belt transport"
about "A named closed loop under broadcast control. Every loaded well driven by a rail channel follows the same shift in a step; the cyclic order of ions is preserved; and docking, splitting or merging is a separate declared operation. Off-loop docks may stay put, but a loaded well on a switchless rail may not. This is the website's standard machine with no transport rule removed."

include "standard"
